  <notes>
    Escalation trigger did NOT fire: verified on Microsoft Learn (2026-10-04) that `Word.Document.onParagraphAdded`
    / `onParagraphChanged` / `onParagraphDeleted` are GA (not preview) under requirement set WordApi 1.6, supported
    on Word on the web / Windows / Mac since build 2308 (Aug 2023) and iPad since 16.76 — well below the "desktop
    2501+" floor, so a GA event exists on every platform this add-in targets. Implemented all 7 steps directionally;
    the only POML-undirected decision was suppressing the locked name box's own "Save as new document" button
    whenever the error banner is already offering the identical action (a refused version save), to avoid showing
    the same button twice. Full writeup, verification sources, gate numbers and the Step 9.5 review table:
    `projects/spaarkeai-word-add-in-r1/notes/094-saved-state-follow-up.md`. Live AC9 (UAT round 4) is OPEN — no
    Office host available in this session, per the POML's own "if unavailable, leave open."
  </notes>
